# Keep the function bundle to what actually serves a request. Vercel builds
# one Python function from api/ and installs dependencies from
# pyproject.toml; everything listed below is dev-only or never read at
# request time, and each megabyte here is cold-start latency on every
# invocation.
#
# The parent engine shipped a deployment that excluded `scripts/` on the
# assumption a directory named that way was dev-only tooling — its content
# store did `from scripts.seed import seed_assets` at request time, so every
# route (including its own 404 handler) raised `ModuleNotFoundError` and the
# site returned 500 for everything. `tests/test_deployment_scaffolding.py`
# checks this file against what `vsm/` and `api/` actually import, so that
# mistake fails a test here instead of costing a deploy cycle.

tests/
docs/
.superpowers/
.claude/
.impeccable/
.git/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
var/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
Makefile
README.md
PRODUCT.md
.env.example

# NOT ignored, and each for a reason a future edit should not undo:
#   vsm/             the application — including vsm/ui/templates (read by
#                     Jinja2's FileSystemLoader) and vsm/ui/static (served by
#                     StaticFiles) at request time, not just vsm/*.py.
#   api/              the Vercel entrypoint itself.
#   pyproject.toml    Vercel installs dependencies from this file; there is
#                     no requirements.txt in this repo to fall back to.
